.TH AVR\-CACHE\-DELETE 1 "" "avr 0.1.4" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-cache-delete \- Delete cache entries by key name or all entries.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr cache delete
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Delete cache entries by key name or all entries.
.PP
Exactly one of --key or --all must be provided. When using --key, --type is required to scope the deletion.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
Examples:
    avr cache delete --repo rep-abc123 --type gha --key "node_modules" --ref refs/heads/main --yes
    avr cache delete --repo rep-abc123 --all --yes
.fi
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-repo\fR \fITEXT\fR
Repository (org/repo or rep-xxx). Auto-detected from git remote if omitted.
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID or slug. Uses default org if not specified (see: avr config set org).
.TP
\fB\-\-type\fR \fITEXT\fR
Cache type (required with --key, e.g. gha, bazel, sccache).
.TP
\fB\-\-key\fR \fITEXT\fR
Delete entries matching this cache key name.
.TP
\fB\-\-ref\fR \fITEXT\fR
Ref to narrow deletion scope (used by gha).
.TP
\fB\-\-all\fR
Delete ALL cache entries for the repository.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR, \fB\-y\fR
Skip confirmation prompt.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR avr (1),
.BR avr-cache (1),
.BR avr-cache-list (1),
.BR avr-cache-usage (1)
